3
00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:26.472
<v NARRATOR>Sprig is a small sapling-tween. Her body is visibly branched, with two main forks that split into smaller branches.

4
00:00:26.472 --> 00:00:35.883
<v NARRATOR>Her branches are always shifting, not with the wind, but with her choices. They move in coordinated opposition.

5
00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:43.894
<v SPRIG>I am Sprig. I am a branching sapling. My body physically changes when I choose a direction.

6
00:00:43.894 --> 00:00:50.945
<v SPRIG>This is how I know a choice has weight. My branches re-route to express it.

7
00:00:50.945 --> 00:00:58.436
<v NARRATOR>In branching dialogue, every choice should re-route the story in a way the reader can feel.

8
00:00:58.436 --> 00:01:08.247
<v SPRIG>Choices that lead to identical outcomes are unweighted and feel hollow. My branches would not move for them.

9
00:01:08.247 --> 00:01:15.538
<v NARRATOR>She grew up in a small grove, where an AI dialogue coach named Patter found her.

10
00:01:15.538 --> 00:01:25.549
<v NARRATOR>He had been frustrated by dialogue trees where every branch led to the same place. He asked her to demonstrate a choice.

11
00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:35.240
<v SPRIG>Watch. I choose left. My left fork grows. My right fork shortens. My body has re-routed.

12
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:43.051
<v NARRATOR>Patter saw it then. A meaningful choice physically changes the structure of what comes next.

13
00:01:43.051 --> 00:01:51.862
<v SPRIG>A branch that does not re-route the sapling is not a branch. It is just a twig pointing nowhere.

14
00:01:51.862 --> 00:02:00.673
<v NARRATOR>A choice with weight re-routes the story. That is the whole principle. That is what makes a branch meaningful.

15
